bout dark omens.","timing":{"repeat":"Every 40 turns"},"trigger":"Tribe Cleared","weight":1},{"author":"Andy Auseon","id":"EVENTSTORY_TRIBE_CULT_OF_FLAME","name":"Cult of Flame","options":[{"outcomes":[{"rewards":[{"text":"Opinion memory"},{"text":"+1 Happiness level"},{"text":"Law-based opinion shift"}]}],"raw":{"bonuses":[{"fields":["Memory MEMORYTRIBE_RESPECT"],"id":"BONUS_EVENTOPTION_TRIBE_CULT_OF_FLAME_KEEP","pct":null,"weight":null},{"fields":["iHappinessLevels 1"],"id":"BONUS_HAPPINESS_UP","pct":null,"weight":null},{"fields":["aiLawOpinion: LAW_MONOTHEISM=-40"],"id":"BONUS_EVENTOPTION_TRIBE_CULT_OF_FLAME_POLY_FAMILY","pct":null,"weight":null}],"gates":[]},"requirements":[],"text":"Install them in a city to show tolerance."},{"outcomes":[{"rewards":[{"text":"+4 Legitimacy"},{"text":"Law-based opinion shift"}]}],"raw":{"bonuses":[{"fields":["iLegitimacy 4"],"id":"BONUS_EVENTOPTION_TRIBE_CULT_OF_FLAME_SMASH","pct":null,"weight":null},{"fields":["aiLawOpinion: LAW_POLYTHEISM=-20"],"id":"BONUS_EVENTOPTION_TRIBE_CULT_OF_FLAME_MONO_FAMILY","pct":null,"weight":null}],"gates":[]},"requirements":[],"text":"Deface them and smash them to dust."}],"subjects":["Tribe","Leader Us","Unit Us","Family Us","Tile"],"text":"Scholars at the site of the [tribe]' defeat discover shrines, carvings, and statues depicting the worship of fire. They believe these treasures are associated with the Cult of Flame, an ancient tribal religion still practiced by many of our subjects. The cult's icons are sacred to its followers, so we should proceed with caution.","timing":{"repeat":"Once per game"},"trigger":"Tribe Cleared","weight":3},{"author":"Andy Auseon","id":"EVENTSTORY_TRIBE_EXOTIC_INFLUENCE","name":"Exotic Influence","options":[{"outcomes":[{"rewards":[{"text":"Opinion memory"},{"text":"+2 Legitimacy"}]}],"raw":{"bonuses":[{"fields":["Memory MEMORYTRIBE_INSULTED_CUSTOMS"],"id":"BONUS_EVENTOPTION_TRIBE_EXOTIC_INFLUENCE_OPTION_0","pct":null,"weight":null},{"fields":["iLegitimacy 2"],"id":"BONUS_EVENTOPTION_TRIBE_EXOTIC_INFLUENCE_OPTION_0_CHARACTER","pct":null,"weight":null}],"gates":[]},"requirements":[],"text":"I will not be tainted by these savages."},{"outcomes":[{"rewards":[{"text":"Opinion memory"},{"text":"-2 Legitimacy"},{"text":"Gain trait: Regalia of the Conqueror","tip":["As leader: +40 Tribal Leader Opinions"],"tipTitle":"Regalia of the Conqueror — trait"}]}],"raw":{"bonuses":[{"fields":["Memory MEMORYTRIBE_ACCEPTED_CUSTOMS"],"id":"BONUS_EVENTOPTION_TRIBE_EXOTIC_INFLUENCE_OPTION_1","pct":null,"weight":null},{"fields":["iLegitimacy -2","aeAddTraits: TRAIT_REGALIA_OF_THE_CONQUERER"],"id":"BONUS_EVENTOPTION_TRIBE_EXOTIC_INFLUENCE_OPTION_1_CHARACTER","pct":null,"weight":null}],"gates":[]},"requirements":[],"text":"These prizes are mine by right and rule."},{"outcomes":[{"rewards":[{"text":"Opinion memory"},{"base":160,"per":40,"text":"+160 Money (+40/city)","yield":"money"}]}],"raw":{"bonuses":[{"fields":["Memory MEMORYTRIBE_INSULTED_CUSTOMS"],"id":"BONUS_EVENTOPTION_TRIBE_EXOTIC_INFLUENCE_OPTION_2","pct":null,"weight":null},{"fields":["aiGlobalYieldsBase: YIELD_MONEY=160","aiGlobalYieldsPer: YIELD_MONEY=40"],"id":"BONUS_MONEY_GAIN_AVERAGE","pct":null,"weight":null}],"gates":[]},"requirements":[],"text":"Put these treasures in our nation's coffers."},{"outcomes":[{"rewards":[{"text":"Opinion memory"},{"text":"+4 Legitimacy"}]}],"raw":{"bonuses":[{"fields":["Memory MEMORYTRIBE_ACCEPTED_CUSTOMS"],"id":"BONUS_EVENTOPTION_TRIBE_EXOTIC_INFLUENCE_OPTION_3","pct":null,"weight":null},{"fields":["iLegitimacy 4"],"id":"BONUS_EVENTOPTION_TRIBE_EXOTIC_INFLUENCE_OPTION_3_CHARACTER","pct":null,"weight":null}],"gates":[{"tag":"LeaderSubject","values":["SUBJECT_BLESSED"]}]},"requirements":[],"text":"This piece bears the crest of one of our ancient heros! I shall wear it proudly!"}],"subjects":["Tribe","Leader Us","Tile"],"text":"In an act of supplication, the surviving [tribe] nobles offer you a wealth of jewelry, fineries, and icons representing their culture. As conqueror, you are expected to wear this traditional raiment. Our generals grumble behind your back, but there is wisdom in appealing to the newly vanquished.","timing":{"repeat":"Every 40 turns"},"trigger":"Tribe Cleared","weight":2},{"author":"Velociryx","conditions":["General","Leader Nebuchadnezzar I","Player Babylonia","Player Two Tribes Cleared"],"dlc":"Wonders & Dynasties","id":"EVENTSTORY_FOR_THE_GLORY_OF_BABYLON","name":"For the Glory of Babylon","options":[{"outcomes":[{"rewards":[{"base":50,"per":15,"text":"+50 Stone (+15/city)","yield":"stone"}]}],"raw":{"bonuses":[{"fields":["aiGlobalYieldsBase: YIELD_STONE=50","aiGlobalYieldsPer: YIELD_STONE=15"],"id":"BONUS_STONE_GAIN_AVERAGE","pct":null,"weight":null}],"gates":[]},"requirements":[],"text":"Dismantle their villages and rip down their edifices, bringing the stone back to Babylon for the furtherance of our national goals."},{"outcomes":[{"rewards":[{"base":60,"per":15,"text":"+60 Civics (+15/city)","yield":"civics"}]}],"raw":{"bonuses":[{"fields":["aiGlobalYieldsBase: YIELD_CIVICS=60","aiGlobalYieldsPer: YIELD_CIVICS=15"],"id":"BONUS_CIVICS_GAIN_AVERAGE","pct":null,"weight":null}],"gates":[]},"requirements":[],"text":"Seek out the most talented members of this conquered tribe and bring them back to our lands to help with administrative tasks."}],"pack":"Wonders and Dynasties","prob":30,"subjects":["Tile Tribe Site","Leader Us","Player Us"],"text":"While your first territorial conquest could have been seen as a fluke or a stroke of luck, your continued success proves otherwise. There is truly nothing you cannot accomplish. Now is the time to demonstrate your brilliance for the world to see. What shall be the fate of this new land?","timing":{"repeat":"Once per game"},"trigger":"Tribe Cleared","weight":4},{"author":"Andy Auseon","conditions":["Tribe Scythians","Tribe Numidians"],"id":"EVENTSTORY_TRIBE_HORSE_LORDS","name":"Horse Lords","options":[{"outcomes":[{"rewards":[{"text":"+1 Horse Archer"}]}],"raw":{"bonuses":[{"fields":["aiUnits: UNIT_HORSE_ARCHER=1"],"id":"BONUS_EVENTOPTION_TRIBE_HORSE_LORDS_OPTION_0","pct":null,"weight":null}],"gates":[]},"requirements":[],"text":"Teach riders how to shoot."},{"outcomes":[{"rewards":[{"text":"+1 Horseman"}]}],"raw":{"bonuses":[{"fields":["aiUnits: UNIT_HORSEMAN=1"],"id":"BONUS_EVENTOPTION_TRIBE_HORSE_LORDS_OPTION_1","pct":null,"weight":null}],"gates":[]},"requirements":[],"text":"Our warriors need mounts."},{"outcomes":[{"rewards":[]}],"raw":{"bonuses":[{"fields":["aeForceResources: RESOURCE_HORSE"],"id":"BONUS_EVENTOPTION_TRIBE_HORSE_LORDS_OPTION_2","pct":null,"weight":null}],"gates":[]},"requirements":[],"text":"Field animals are in short supply."}],"subjects":["Tribe","Leader Us","Tile","Tech Spoked Wheel Discovered Us","City Us"],"text":"The fallen [tribe] stronghold includes sophisticated stables and a herd of healthy, trained horses. The animals look well fed and unharmed. How shall we utilize these animals?","timing":{"repeat":"Once per game"},"trigger":"Tribe Cleared","weight":3},{"author":"Andy Auseon","id":"EVENTSTORY_TRIBE_LIBERATED","name":"Liberated","options":[{"outcomes":[{"rewards":[]}],"raw":{"bonuses":[{"fields":["iCitizens 1"],"id":"BONUS_ADD_CITIZEN_1","pct":null,"weight":null}],"gates":[]},"requirements":[],"text":"Let them return to their families."},{"outcomes":[{"rewards":[{"text":"-1 Happiness level"},{"text":"+1 Heavy Infantry unit"}]}],"raw":{"bonuses":[{"fields":["iHappinessLevels -1"],"id":"BONUS_HAPPINESS_DOWN","pct":null,"weight":null},{"fields":["aiBonusUnits: BONUSUNITCLASS_HEAVY_INFANTRY=1"],"id":"BONUS_EVENTOPTION_TRIBE_LIBERATED_OPTION_1","pct":null,"weight":null}],"gates":[]},"requirements":[],"text":"Arm them and put them at the front."}],"subjects":["Tribe","City Us","Tile"],"text":"A crumbling prison stands in the [tribe] settlement. Scores of soldiers and citizens from [rival] have been languishing here for years, most believed dead by their loved ones. Their release calls 